    "created_at": "2026-10-02T09:17:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-02T09:17:13Z",
    "body": "> If this matches current implementations, that satisfies the implementer interest item.\r\n\r\nWell, it _kind of_ matches implementations. No implementation ships `close` (Chrome did implement it, but it's behind I believe a test-only flag).\r\n\r\nHowever all implementation disagree on GC semantics, which this PR restores to the pre-close-event state. None implemented the post-close-event GC behavior, and only Firefox has the old one.\r\n\r\n> Should have tests to verify the lack of an event and event handler IDL attribute.\r\n\r\nDone",
